    {
        "name": "Feline Chronic Bronchitis",
        "name_ja": "猫慢性気管支炎",
        "symptoms": {"coughing", "wheezing", "labored_breathing", "exercise_intolerance", "nasal_discharge"},
        "description": "A chronic, non-allergic, neutrophilic inflammatory airway disease distinct from feline asthma. Characterized by chronic cough (>2 months), bronchial wall thickening, and mucus hypersecretion without IgE-mediated bronchospasm. BAL shows neutrophilic predominance (>7%, typically without significant eosinophilia). Reversible component is minimal — bronchodilator response usually limited compared to asthma. Often coexists with chronic infection (Mycoplasma spp., Bordetella bronchiseptica, secondary bacterial colonization).",
        "description_ja": "猫喘息とは異なる慢性・非アレルギー性・好中球性炎症性気道疾患。慢性咳嗽（>2ヶ月）、気管支壁肥厚、粘液過分泌を特徴とし、IgE介在性気管支攣縮を伴わない。BALで好中球優位（>7%、通常は好酸球増多なし）。可逆性要素は最小限—気管支拡張薬への反応は喘息と比べ限定的。慢性感染（Mycoplasma属、Bordetella bronchiseptica、二次的細菌定着）の併発が多い。",
        "urgency": "moderate",
        "recommended_tests": ["chest_xray", "bronchoalveolar_lavage", "complete_blood_count", "heartworm_antigen"],
        "causes": "Idiopathic in most cases. Contributing factors: chronic environmental irritants (cigarette smoke, cooking aerosols, scented products, low-quality litter dust), chronic low-grade airway infection (Mycoplasma felis the most common bacterial isolate from feline BAL — present in 25-50% of bronchitis cases), inhaled allergens (overlap with asthma in some cats), recurrent silent aspiration (LES dysfunction), obesity. Differential includes heartworm-associated respiratory disease (HARD), pulmonary parasites (Aelurostrongylus abstrusus), neoplasia (pulmonary carcinoma), pulmonary fibrosis (rare in cats).",
        "causes_ja": "多くは特発性。寄与因子：慢性環境刺激物（タバコの煙、調理時のエアロゾル、香り付き製品、低品質猫砂の粉塵）、慢性軽度気道感染（Mycoplasma felisが猫BALで最多分離菌—気管支炎症例の25-50%）、吸入アレルゲン（喘息との重複あり）、反復性の無症候性誤嚥（下部食道括約筋機能不全）、肥満。鑑別：フィラリア関連呼吸器疾患（HARD）、肺寄生虫（Aelurostrongylus abstrusus）、腫瘍（肺癌）、肺線維症（猫では稀）。",
        "pathophysiology": "Chronic airway inflammation drives goblet cell hyperplasia, submucosal gland hypertrophy, and neutrophilic infiltration. Persistent insult leads to bronchial wall thickening, smooth muscle hypertrophy, and reduced mucociliary clearance. Unlike asthma, bronchospasm is mild or absent; the predominant problem is mucus plugging and chronic inflammation rather than reversible airway obstruction. Mycoplasma colonization perpetuates inflammation by impairing ciliary function and triggering ongoing neutrophil recruitment. Long-term: airway remodeling, possible bronchiectasis development, increased susceptibility to acute bacterial pneumonia. Substance P / NK1-R signaling sensitizes cough reflex (rationale for off-label maropitant adjunct, similar to canine bronchitis).",
        "pathophysiology_ja": "気道の慢性炎症が杯細胞過形成、粘膜下腺肥厚、好中球浸潤を促進。持続的刺激により気管支壁肥厚、平滑筋肥厚、粘液線毛クリアランス低下。喘息と異なり気管支攣縮は軽度または不在；主病態は可逆性気道閉塞ではなく粘液栓塞と慢性炎症。Mycoplasma感染は線毛機能を阻害し好中球動員を持続させ炎症を慢性化。長期：気道リモデリング、気管支拡張症の発生可能性、急性細菌性肺炎への感受性増加。サブスタンスP/NK1-Rシグナルが咳反射を感作（犬と同様、適応外マロピタント補助療法の根拠）。",
        "treatment": "DIAGNOSTIC WORKUP (essential for differentiating from asthma): (1) Thoracic radiographs (3-view): bronchointerstitial pattern, donut/tram-track airway thickening; less hyperinflation than asthma. (2) CBC: typically no eosinophilia. (3) Heartworm antigen + antibody testing. (4) Fecal Baermann (Aelurostrongylus). (5) Bronchoscopy + BAL with cytology and aerobic + Mycoplasma culture (definitive): >7% neutrophils confirms bronchitis vs >17% eosinophils for asthma. TREATMENT: (A) ANTI-INFLAMMATORY (cornerstone): prednisolone 1-2 mg/kg PO q12h × 5-7 days, then taper to 0.5 mg/kg q24h, then 0.25-0.5 mg/kg EOD (lowest effective). Use prednisolone, NOT prednisone (poor conversion in cats). (B) INHALED CORTICOSTEROIDS: fluticasone 110 μg via AeroKat spacer q12h for long-term control with fewer systemic effects; allow 7-14 days for full effect (oral steroid bridge during initiation). (C) ANTIMICROBIALS (when indicated): doxycycline 5-10 mg/kg PO q12-24h × 4-6 weeks for confirmed/suspected Mycoplasma (also has anti-inflammatory immunomodulatory effect). Always follow with water bolus or wet food (esophageal stricture risk in cats with dry doxycycline tablets). Azithromycin 5-10 mg/kg PO q24h for 5 days then EOD as alternative. Pradofloxacin 7.5 mg/kg PO q24h for resistant cases. (D) BRONCHODILATORS (limited benefit but useful in bronchospasm component): terbutaline 0.625-1.25 mg PO q12h, or albuterol 90 μg via AeroKat 2 puffs q6-12h PRN. Avoid theophylline in cats (narrow therapeutic window, side effects). (E) ANTITUSSIVES for cough control: butorphanol 0.2-0.4 mg/kg PO q8-12h. Maropitant 1 mg/kg PO q24h × 5 days has anecdotal antitussive benefit (less established than canine evidence; off-label). (F) MUCOLYTICS: nebulized saline 5 mL q8-12h via face mask + chest coupage to mobilize secretions. N-acetylcysteine inhaled or oral controversial. (G) WEIGHT MANAGEMENT: BCS 5/9 critical; obesity worsens dyspnea and reduces drug efficacy. (H) ENVIRONMENT: low-dust litter, smoke elimination, HEPA filter, avoid scented products. ACUTE EXACERBATION: oxygen, IV/IM dexamethasone SP 0.1-0.2 mg/kg, terbutaline 0.01 mg/kg SC, broad-spectrum antibiotics if pneumonia suspected. MONITORING: thoracic radiographs at 3-6 months, then yearly; recheck respiratory exam q3-6mo; trend cough frequency (owner log) and exercise tolerance.",
        "treatment_ja": "診断ワークフロー（喘息との鑑別に必須）：(1)胸部X線3方向：気管支間質性パターン、ドーナツ/トラムトラック様気道壁肥厚；喘息より肺過膨張は軽度。(2)CBC：通常好酸球増多なし。(3)フィラリア抗原＋抗体検査。(4)糞便ベルマン法（Aelurostrongylus）。(5)気管支鏡＋BAL（細胞診＋好気性培養＋Mycoplasma培養、確定診断）：好中球>7%で気管支炎、好酸球>17%で喘息。治療：(A)抗炎症（基幹）：プレドニゾロン1-2 mg/kg PO q12h ×5-7日、その後0.5 mg/kg q24hに漸減、最終0.25-0.5 mg/kg EOD（最小有効量）。プレドニゾロンを使用（猫はプレドニゾン変換不良）。(B)吸入ステロイド：フルチカゾン110 μgをAeroKatでq12h、長期管理で全身副作用少；十分な効果に7-14日（導入時は経口ブリッジ）。(C)抗菌薬（適応時）：ドキシサイクリン5-10 mg/kg PO q12-24h ×4-6週（Mycoplasma確認/疑い、抗炎症的免疫調節作用も）。乾燥錠剤は食道狭窄リスクのため必ず水または濡れフードと一緒に投与。代替はアジスロマイシン5-10 mg/kg PO q24h ×5日後にEOD、耐性例にはプラドフロキサシン7.5 mg/kg PO q24h。(D)気管支拡張薬（効果限定的だが気管支攣縮要素に有用）：テルブタリン0.625-1.25 mg PO q12h、サルブタモール90 μgをAeroKatで2吸入q6-12h頓用。猫ではテオフィリン回避（治療域狭・副作用）。(E)鎮咳薬：ブトルファノール0.2-0.4 mg/kg PO q8-12h。マロピタント1 mg/kg PO q24h ×5日に逸話的鎮咳効果（犬よりエビデンス弱・適応外）。(F)粘液溶解：生食ネブライザー5 mL q8-12hをマスクで＋カパージュで分泌物動員。N-アセチルシステインの吸入・経口は議論あり。(G)体重管理：BCS 5/9が重要；肥満は呼吸困難を悪化させ薬剤効果を低下。(H)環境：低粉塵猫砂、禁煙、HEPA、香り付き製品回避。急性増悪：酸素、デキサメタゾンSP 0.1-0.2 mg/kg IV/IM、テルブタリン0.01 mg/kg SC、肺炎疑いで広域抗菌薬。モニタリング：3-6ヶ月後・以降年1回の胸部X線；3-6ヶ月毎の呼吸器評価；咳頻度（飼い主ログ）と運動耐容能の推移。",
        "prevention": "Eliminate cigarette smoke (most modifiable factor). Use low-dust litter (paper, pine, silica gel — avoid clay/clumping dust). Avoid air fresheners, scented candles, aerosol cleaners, perfumes. HEPA air filter in primary living area. Maintain BCS 5/9. Heartworm prophylaxis in endemic regions. Treat upper respiratory infections promptly to prevent chronic bronchial colonization. Indoor-only lifestyle to reduce environmental exposures.",
        "prevention_ja": "禁煙（最も修正可能な因子）。低粉塵猫砂を使用（紙・木・シリカゲル—粘土系・凝固系を避ける）。芳香剤・香り付きキャンドル・エアロゾル洗剤・香水を避ける。主な生活域のHEPA空気清浄機。BCS 5/9を維持。流行地域ではフィラリア予防。慢性気管支定着を防ぐため上気道感染を迅速治療。環境曝露軽減のため屋内飼育。",
        "prognosis": "Long-term management with appropriate ICS + environmental control: good prognosis with normal QOL in most cats; lifespan typically not shortened in mild-moderate disease. Mycoplasma-confirmed cases often improve significantly with extended doxycycline therapy. Refractory cases or those progressing to bronchiectasis: variable; recurrent pneumonia is common cause of mortality. Predictors of good outcome: smoke elimination, weight loss, owner adherence to inhaled therapy, addressing Mycoplasma. References: Reinero CR. Vet J 2011 (lower airway disease); Foster SF & Martin P. JFMS 2011 (bronchial disease in cats); Trzil JE. Vet Clin North Am Small Anim Pract 2020; Padrid PA. AAFP 2014 guidelines.",
        "prognosis_ja": "適切な吸入ステロイド＋環境管理で長期管理した場合：多くの猫で予後良好、正常なQOL；軽中等症では寿命短縮なし。Mycoplasma確認例はドキシサイクリン延長療法で著明改善することが多い。難治例や気管支拡張症へ進行した症例：経過は変動、反復性肺炎が主な死因。予後良好因子：禁煙、減量、吸入療法の遵守、Mycoplasma対処。参考文献：Reinero CR. Vet J 2011（下気道疾患）；Foster SF & Martin P. JFMS 2011（猫の気管支疾患）；Trzil JE. Vet Clin North Am Small Anim Pract 2020；Padrid PA. AAFP 2014ガイドライン。",
        "onset_pattern": {"chronic", "subacute"},
        "age_predisposition": {"adult", "senior"},
    },
